# Dash on the Pier (worlds/01_PIER.md, Key 1): the race from the gate to the end of the pier, and her crop.
# levels/pier/keys/dash_race.gd runs the race; "set pier/race_go" starts it. Every joke is the owner's to review.

~ start
[if pier/race_won] => after
[if pier/race_on] => waiting
[if pier/race_lost] => rematch
Dash [grin]: There she is. Vesper's new climber.
Nim: Nim.
Dash: Dash. Fastest thing in the Old Quarter, on two legs or four.
Dash: Here's the deal. Beat me from the gate to the end of the pier, and you get my crop.
Nim: And if I lose?
Dash: You don't get my crop. And I tell everyone.
- You're on. => go
- Not now. => later

~ go
Dash [grin]: The gate. I'll count us in.
set pier/race_go
=> END

~ later
Dash: Scared. Understandable.
=> END

~ waiting
Dash: The gate, Nim. The big pink one. You can't miss it.

~ rematch
Dash [grin]: Back for more? Same deal. Gate to the end.
- Again. => go
- Not now. => later

~ won
Dash [shock]: ...Huh.
Nim: I won.
Dash: You won because I let you win. Obviously. For morale.
Nim: You vaulted a fence.
Dash: I was warming up.
Dash: Fine. A deal's a deal. Hold your strike and it cracks. Bells, switches, targets, gulls.
Dash: Goons too, in the garb. Not in the suit. That's just tacky.
=> END

~ after
Dash: That shooting gallery on the Midway's rigged, by the way. And nobody's ever rung the bell on the striker. Have fun.

# The first time Nim comes out of Dash's hut in the Domme suit: how the suit works (worlds/01_PIER.md "How it
# teaches" 3-4). Player mechanics, said by Dash (owner, on the Deck: nothing taught cover). dash_race.gd plays it.
~ suit
Dash [grin]: Need a hand with the buttons? ...Yeah, no. Claws. You're on your own.
Dash: Right. In that, nobody sees a burglar. They see someone who belongs here.
Dash: So act like it. Walk. Slow, chin up, like the pier owes you money.
Dash: Run, jump, climb a wall, start a scrap where people can see? They notice. That's your Composure going.
Dash: Lose it all and your cover's blown. Every goon in shouting distance comes running.
Nim: And then?
Dash: Then you get out of sight and let them forget your face. Or change back at a wardrobe.
Dash: Strutting about in plain view puts it back. So does being obeyed.
Dash [grin]: And with that look, try telling someone to kneel. See what happens.
=> END
